# Engine files that include a shell header.
#
# ONE ENTRY, and it is not debt. types.h -> tune.h is deliberate: the include
# sits after types.h's own #endif so the SPSA macros reach anywhere types.h
# does, and removing it would make every future tuning run add an include
# first. See docs/00-architecture.md.
#
# The other three went with B7's seams. Once the option snapshot and the moved
# renderers removed the last symbol references, search.cpp and timeman.cpp were
# including shell headers they no longer used, and the gate's stale-entry
# direction is what said so.
types.h -> tune.h
